% ============================================================================
% angle-types.query.adj — a worked recall over the geometry angle-types library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what makes an angle
% obtuse?": it states no geometry fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against
% the `angle_condition` rows and returns the defining condition + the table's
% source/locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the
% condition `equals_90`, recall its angle type — right). A word that is not one
% of the five angle types abstains honestly — the engine never invents a
% condition.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli angle-types.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "angle-types.adj"

? angle_condition(acute, $Condition)      % expect between_0_and_90
? angle_condition(obtuse, $Condition)     % expect between_90_and_180
? angle_condition(reflex, $Condition)     % expect greater_than_180
? angle_condition($Type, equals_90)       % reverse bind — expect right
? angle_condition(circle, $Condition)     % expect abstain — a circle is not one of the five angle types
